          <type>const Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor33t&lt; T &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>dGp</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the incremental plastic deformation gradient from the plastic velocity gradient using the exponential map, evaluated by scaling and squaring.</para>
<para>The result is that of <ref refid="_marmot_finite_strain_plasticity_8h_1a9381b95ec8a254156bf56ae7d21e11cd" kindref="member">exponentialMap()</ref>, but the series is only evaluated for <formula id="53">$ \Delta\boldsymbol{G}^p / 2^s $</formula> with <formula id="54">$ |\Delta\boldsymbol{G}^p| / 2^s \leq 1/2 $</formula>, and then squared <formula id="55">$ s $</formula> times,   <formula id="56">\[  \exp( \Delta\boldsymbol{G}^p ) = \left( \exp( \Delta\boldsymbol{G}^p / 2^s ) \right)^{2^s}.
\]</formula> For <formula id="57">$ |\Delta\boldsymbol{G}^p| \leq 1/2 $</formula>, <formula id="58">$ s = 0 $</formula> and the result is identical to that of <ref refid="_marmot_finite_strain_plasticity_8h_1a9381b95ec8a254156bf56ae7d21e11cd" kindref="member">exponentialMap()</ref>. Larger increments, e.g. those of the intermediate iterates of a return mapping, are represented as well, where the truncated series of <ref refid="_marmot_finite_strain_plasticity_8h_1a9381b95ec8a254156bf56ae7d21e11cd" kindref="member">exponentialMap()</ref> fails.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Scalar type, real or complex (the scaling is chosen from the real part). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>dGp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Incremental plastic velocity gradient. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Incremental plastic deformation gradient. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
